pageType: content
background:
  type: image
  src: media/template-white.png
  fit: {mode: fill}
notes: |
  Timing: about 60 seconds.

  The final image returns to Las Meninas through a style-transfer workflow. The content image supplies the figures and room; the project-generated cognitive-map image supplies layered planes, nodes, lines, and a stronger sense of convergence. In the final composition, the painter, large canvas, mirror, doorway, Infanta, attendants, and dog remain recognizable, while the geometry of looking becomes visible on the surface. I also inserted a contemporary viewer into the mirrored position. The transformation is not meant to imitate Velázquez. It makes the relation between room, painting, and viewer more explicit.
